WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.100
Here's the register
you'll check in the lab.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.438
It's the guide's table of lifecycle
rows, kept as reviewed JSON.

3
00:00:06.438 --> 00:00:10.873
Each row is an account-state
transition or an HR-mastered value,

4
00:00:10.873 --> 00:00:15.563
and each names exactly one writer
and, where there is one, a backstop.

5
00:00:15.563 --> 00:00:17.987
Inbound provisioning creates the account.

6
00:00:17.987 --> 00:00:22.268
It enables it at hire, disables it at
separation, and re-enables it if a

7
00:00:22.268 --> 00:00:27.388
separation is cancelled, with Lifecycle
Workflows as the backstop for all three.

8
00:00:27.388 --> 00:00:30.800
It writes the hire date, the
leave date and the manager.

9
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.138
The organization code and worker
type code have the directory sync as

10
00:00:35.138 --> 00:00:39.475
an interim backstop, for synced
users until Active Directory retires.

11
00:00:39.475 --> 00:00:43.600
The card management system's integration
writes the certificate binding.

12
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.211
And notice deletion: the
post-separation workflow writes it,

13
00:00:47.211 --> 00:00:49.450
and inbound provisioning never does.

14
00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.020
The register forbids it.
